# Citation metadata for the GLACE dataset, read by GitHub (R-16). `version`
# is one string with DATASET_VERSION and the two collection documents;
# tests/test_version.py enforces that. `date-released` is written in the release commit itself.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
title: GLACE Alps
abstract: >-
  Annual summer composites of Sentinel-1 12-day repeat-pass InSAR coherence
  (COH12) and radiometrically terrain-corrected backscatter (RTC) over the
  Alpine Convention perimeter, 2015–2026. Composites are locally resolution
  weighted, so each output pixel is dominated by the acquisitions that resolve
  it best rather than by whichever orbit happened to observe it most often. Two
  collections are published: per-tile composites on the 10 m MGRS grid for
  analysis and machine learning, and one annual mosaic per year on a fixed
  equal-area grid (ETRS89-LAEA, 40 m) for mapping, inspection and area
  statistics.
authors:
  - family-names: Gentner
    given-names: Luis Q.
    email: luis.gentner@geo.uzh.ch
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4453-0881
    affiliation: University of Zurich, Department of Geography
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/lqgentner/glace-catalog
url: https://source.coop/giuz/glace-alps
# The DOI of this version, bumped with it; tests/test_version.py checks it
# against metadata/catalog.yaml. The canonical DOI names every version.
doi: 10.48656/60er-3j55
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.48656/d4r9-fj97
    description: Canonical DOI, every version
version: "1.0"
keywords:
  - Sentinel-1
  - SAR
  - InSAR coherence
  - backscatter
  - glaciers
  - cryosphere
  - Alps
  - STAC
